---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { company } from '../../i18n/ui';

const alternates = [
    { lang: 'de', path: '/datenschutz' },
    { lang: 'en', path: '/en/datenschutz' },
];
---
<Base
    lang="en"
    title="Privacy Policy | ALVEX Handel GmbH"
    description="Privacy policy of ALVEX Handel GmbH – how we process personal data in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)."
    alternates={alternates}
    switchHref="/datenschutz"
>
    <main class="section legal-page">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="legal-intro">
                We take the protection of your personal data seriously. This policy explains what data we
                process when you visit this website and contact us, and the rights you have under the EU
                General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
            </p>
            <p class="legal-note">
                This English text is a courtesy translation. The legally binding version of this privacy
                policy is the <a href="/datenschutz">German version</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>1. Controller</h2>
            <p>
                The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:<br>
                {company.name}<br>
                Steinweg 3, 60313 Frankfurt am Main, Germany<br>
                Managing Director: {company.managingDirector}<br>
                Phone: {company.phoneDisplay}<br>
                E-mail: <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>
            </p>

            <h2>2. Scope of data processing</h2>
            <p>
                This website is designed to be data-minimising. It uses no cookies, no tracking, no
                analytics services and loads no content from external third-party servers or content delivery
                networks (CDNs). No user profiles are created and no data is passed to third parties for
                advertising purposes.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Server log files &amp; hosting</h2>
            <p>
                This website is hosted by IONOS SE, Elgendorfer Straße 57, 56410 Montabaur, Germany. When you
                access the site, the hosting provider automatically collects and stores information in server
                log files that your browser transmits. This may include the browser type and version, the
                operating system used, the referrer URL, the host name of the accessing device, the time of
                the server request and the IP address.
            </p>
            <p>
                This data is not merged with other data sources. It is processed on the basis of Article 6 (1)
                (f) GDPR; we have a legitimate interest in the technically error-free presentation and
                security of our website. A data processing agreement pursuant to Article 28 GDPR has been
                concluded with the hosting provider. Log data is stored only for as long as necessary for
                these purposes.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Contact form and e-mail contact</h2>
            <p>
                If you send us an enquiry via the contact form or by e-mail, the details you provide
                (in particular your name, company, e-mail address, phone number and message) will be stored by
                us for the purpose of processing the enquiry and in case of follow-up questions.
            </p>
            <p>
                The legal basis for processing this data is Article 6 (1) (b) GDPR where your request relates
                to the performance of a contract or pre-contractual measures, and otherwise our legitimate
                interest in answering your enquiry pursuant to Article 6 (1) (f) GDPR. We delete this data once
                it is no longer required, unless statutory retention periods (e.g. under commercial or tax law)
                apply.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Data recipients</h2>
            <p>
                Your personal data is only passed on to third parties where this is legally permitted or where
                you have consented. Processors (such as our hosting provider) act only on our instructions and
                are bound by contract in accordance with Article 28 GDPR.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
            <p>
                Under the GDPR you have the right to obtain information about your stored personal data (Art.
                15), to have it corrected (Art. 16) or erased (Art. 17), to restrict its processing (Art. 18),
                to data portability (Art. 20) and to object to processing (Art. 21). Where processing is based
                on consent, you may withdraw that consent at any time with effect for the future. To exercise
                your rights, please contact us using the details in section 1.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
            <p>
                You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. The authority
                responsible for us is:<br>
                Der Hessische Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit,
                Postfach 3163, 65021 Wiesbaden, Germany.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Data security</h2>
            <p>
                This website uses TLS/SSL encryption for security reasons and to protect the transmission of
                confidential content. You can recognise an encrypted connection by the "https://" prefix in
                your browser's address bar.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>
                We reserve the right to amend this privacy policy to ensure it always complies with current
                legal requirements or to reflect changes to our services. The current version applies to your
                next visit.
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>
</Base>
